title: "Quantitative Methods in International Business with Python"
abstract: >-
  A twelve-session graduate course in which every method is derived before it is
  used, and every result is produced on the student's own machine with open
  tools. Covers least squares and its geometry, inference and diagnostics, the
  bias-variance trade-off and cross-validation, penalised regression,
  classification, tree ensembles, PCA and factor models, clustering and text as
  data, double machine learning, and forecasting under drift with a graded
  governance file. Includes a synthetic teaching data spine, ten group research
  mandates across five fixed analytical angles, and an individual-accountability
  scheme for group work.
